# What the next Firebase Test Lab run does. Edit and push to run again.
# (2026-10-25, fifteenth run: the 1.64.75 candidate again, the last two of
# the day's physical tests. In run 40188289751 both phones passed 15 of 16;
# Original failed, a move from ExoPlayer to libmpv that held the picture
# 5.3-6.1 s. Now the Original plays on ExoPlayer too (one MP4 through the
# proxy), and a film that stalls still counts as playing, so a change made
# during a stall no longer opens the next copy paused. Device lab run
# 40192338478: 16 of 17 on a runner line of 1.3-4 Mbit/s — Original, about
# 10 Mbit/s, cannot play on that line; the rest passed.)
# (2026-10-25, fourteenth run: the 1.64.75 candidate on the realme and the
# OPPO. New: the player's messages in a dark pill near the top instead of
# a light bar over the controls; a quality choice that waits out a
# reconnect, and steers the ladder directly if the renewer cannot answer
# (the owner's "Could not switch quality" on Tears of Steel); "Auto ·
# 480p" on the quality button; no dead decoder button on the ladder; the
# lab tries every line of the Quality menu (LAB check tour->…). Device
# lab: run 40184478393, Tears of Steel, 15/15; run 40186513057, Sintel on
# a busy 4G line (4 Mbit/s, 80-200 ms, 0.5 % loss), 17/17.)
# (2026-10-25, thirteenth run: the same 1.64.74 candidate on the realme,
# now the quota is back. OPPO run 40134791827: 10/10 — the grant 1.1 s
# (3.3 s in run 40118247783), the first long seek 0.6 s (1.1 s), two
# pictures on the swipe instead of seven queued, the landing picture held
# 587 ms to the first frame, bind ok 33, no crash.)
# (2026-10-24, twelfth run: the 1.64.74 candidate on the OPPO alone, the
# day's fifth physical test; the realme once the quota is back. New: the
# seek bar's pictures one at a time, the newest next (the swipe asked for
# seven in run 40118247783, the last 1.3-1.5 s late); a far jump shows the
# picture of where it lands until its own frame (LAB check landing); the
# grant asked to run beside the database. Device lab run 40133079214:
# 11/11, three pictures on the swipe instead of eight, the landing picture
# held 793 ms to the first frame, the grant 1.0 s from the US runner
# (2.5-3.5 s before), run in ap-southeast-1 by the edge log.)
# (2026-10-24, eleventh run: the 1.64.73 candidate on the realme and the
# OPPO. New: far jumps land on a keyframe and the rungs share one pool —
# the trail times each ("hls jump", "exo picture after seek"); the seek
# bar's preview pictures (LAB check preview-*), decoded on the phone's own
# decoder; the volume boost and ten retries on ExoPlayer. The five jumps
# must pass as in run 40094466469, and the OPPO's first long seek should
# come down from 3.0 s. Device lab run 40116409244: 9/9, the way back from
# the home screen included (51 frames in 3 s).)
# (2026-10-24, tenth run: the 1.64.72 candidate on the realme and the OPPO —
# catalogue films with a ladder now play on ExoPlayer, as HLS from the
# proxy. The five checks must pass; a change of quality must show no
# stop ("frozen" about 0.2 s, against 4.2 s in run 39972176423) and the
# rung picked must reach the screen ("shown … after"). Device lab, run
# 40092901280: 5/5, frozen 0.24 s, 240p shown after 1.9 s.)
# (2026-10-23, ninth run: the 1.64.71 candidate on the realme and the OPPO.
# New on the phone's side of playback: the stream cache is SEALED with the
# downloads' Keystore cipher — the trail must say "stream cache: a new film,
# sealed" (the real MediaCrypto, not a test's stand-in) and, after the jump
# back, "stream from the phone … sealed" with the picture moving; the five
# checks must pass as before. Also in the build: the account code on paid
# films (Sintel is free, so not drawn here) and Delete my account (not run).
# RESULT, run 39972176423: both phones 5/5, "a new film, sealed" and
# "stream from the phone … sealed" on each, bind ok 124 and 190, no crash.)
# (2026-10-23, eighth run: the realme again, alone. In run 39919163442 the
# OPPO passed all five checks, bind ok 150; the realme's own line ran at
# 1.6-4 Mbit/s and then nearly stopped (no throughput measured for 66 s,
# later stalls at 37-120 kbit/s) — 240p started 57 s after the switch, and
# three checks failed. Its earlier runs had 6-18 Mbit/s and passed. This
# run says whether that was the line or the app.)
# (2026-10-23, seventh run: 1.64.70 candidate on the realme and the OPPO —
# bound grants, every fetch should say bind ok; the jump checks must pass.
# Also in this build: the QR scanner no longer crashes a phone with no usable
# camera (third_party/mobile_scanner), proved in the device lab.)
# (2026-10-22, sixth run: 1.64.70 asks for BOUND grants — the install's
# hash sealed into every token — and sends its install id with every fetch
# of a granted URL; the Worker answers X-Bind: ok|missing|mismatch and, in
# log mode, refuses nothing. The trail's "LAB proxy upstream … bind {…}"
# says what the Worker answered: every fetch should be "ok". On a virtual
# ARM phone: the day's five physical tests are spent.)
# (2026-10-22, fifth run: the stream proxy hands a stretch over when mpv
# steps back into bytes it was just given, and grows parts once a seek's
# picture is in — 7.7 -> 0.9 Worker requests a megabyte on the bench, seeks
# no slower on the netem lines. The trail's "LAB proxy upstream" line says
# what the Worker saw of the phone. The realme alone: the day's other four
# physical tests are spent.)
# (2026-10-22, fourth run: run 39741227453 was the first to change quality
# on a phone — 240p at 361 s and 366 s, back to Auto at 283 s and 294 s,
# never 00:00 — but Auto took 11 s on the realme, 8 of them waiting on the
# server for the copies it already held. A choice between copies now picks
# from the held grant; a check waits six seconds for the picture to move.)
# (2026-10-22, third run: the jump checks now drive the player screen's own
# controller. Run 39206916255 held one read before the screen had mounted,
# with nothing open in it: every change of quality was refused as "cannot be
# renewed" and the swipe seeked live as for a file — no quality change had
# been tried on a phone yet. A check now waits for the position to land
# near the target, not merely past it.)
# (2026-10-19, second run: the same checks, now waiting for the picture to
# MOVE after each jump and timing it — the first run passed a film stuck at
# the seek target for 45 s. The Worker now mends the chapter track's stray
# sidx that made every seek read the whole film; the app reopens at the
# right moment and does not take a seek's fill for a stall.)
# (2026-10-19: MODE=stream — Sintel through the real API on a realme C53 and
# an OPPO A38, with the jump checks of lib/app.dart: a seek, a change of
# quality, a +30 s skip, a swipe back, back to Auto, each checked for where
# it landed ("LAB check … PASS|FAIL"). 1.64.68 reopened at 00:00 after a
# quality change and after a slow seek.)
# (2026-10-15: MODE=crawl — this branch, the 1.64.64 candidate, crawled by
# Robo for ten minutes on a realme C53 and an OPPO A38: any crash, any
# "Something didn't load" card, on phones people in Myanmar carry. The
# Infinix and TECNO of 11 Oct sat in Test Lab's queue for 90 minutes.)
# (2026-10-11: Infinix and TECNO, which the 10 Oct run did not reach; the
# free test film through the real API on phones Myanmar
# carries — realme, OPPO, Infinix, TECNO, and the 32-bit build on an old
# Samsung — after the fix for the launch address that kept every game loop
# on "Route not found".)
#
# Physical phones, as "model,android-version". The free (Spark) plan allows
# five physical-device tests a day; each line here is one. The workflow
# writes the full list of models Test Lab has into the results, so this can
# be changed to what Myanmar actually carries.
DEVICES="RE58C2,35 OP5759L1,34"
# Phones that run 32-bit Android (MODE=playback or stream): they get the
# armeabi-v7a lab build, in a matrix of their own, since the arm64 APK does
# not install on them (the Galaxy A10 answered "Incompatible Architecture"
# in run 37967931084). They count against the same five a day.
DEVICES32=""
# Which release to test: "latest" or a tag such as v1.64.49-362.
APK_TAG=v1.64.49-362
# How long Robo may explore after the scripted part, in seconds.
TIMEOUT=600
# The phone's language for the run (my = Burmese).
LOCALE=my
# What the run does:
#   robo     — the released APK (APK_TAG), crawled by Robo after the script.
#   playback — this branch built as an arm64 lab APK; Test Lab's game loop
#              plays a pushed 720p film three ways (HW copy-back, HW direct,
#              software), ~50 s each, while CpuProbe logs every thread.
#              A25 (Exynos) and A34 (Dimensity, Android 16) draw with Vulkan;
#              A03s (MediaTek on Android 13) with OpenGL ES.
#              Two game-loop scenarios per phone: 1 = SurfaceTexture video
#              output, 2 = SurfaceProducer (1.64.54), same film, same script.
#   crawl    — this branch as an arm64 lab APK, crawled by Robo after
#              ROBO_SCRIPT (default robo/movies.json; start.json only steps
#              past the introduction and opens the Video tab's ⋮).
#   stream   — this branch as an arm64 lab APK; game-loop scenario 3 plays
#              STREAM_TITLE (a FREE catalogue title) the way a viewer's tap
#              does — request-playback, the Worker, R2, Auto's rung, the
#              proxy — on the phone's own connection, for four minutes.
MODE=stream
# MODE=robo / crawl: the Robo script that runs before the crawl.
ROBO_SCRIPT=test_device/robo/start.json
# Set to an earlier run's id to only collect its results again from Test
# Lab's bucket (BUCKET) — no test is run and no quota is spent. Empty = run.
FETCH_RUN=
BUCKET=test-lab-a83h77c3x52vk-yvsvq7a2052yz
# MODE=stream: the catalogue title to play (Sintel, the free test film).
STREAM_TITLE=0839dacb-59ae-4c95-9279-4901b925965d
